# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the CPU, memory, and GPU resources for a managed workflow, and define sizes that match the size of the problem."
msgstr "Choisis les ressources CPU, mémoire et GPU d'un workflow géré, et définis des tailles adaptées à la taille du problème."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a compute profile"
msgstr "Choisir un profil de calcul"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a compute profile {#choose-a-compute-profile}"
msgstr "Choisir un profil de calcul {#choose-a-compute-profile}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Managed workflows run on compute profiles. A compute profile is a fixed combination of vCPUs, memory, and GPUs, similar to the resources that you request from an HPC scheduler. When you upload a workflow, you map its sizes, such as `S` and `M`, to profiles, and each run picks one of those sizes. The job then runs on its own node with that profile, and keeps the profile until the job ends.\n"
msgstr "Les workflows gérés s'exécutent sur des profils de calcul. Un profil de calcul est une combinaison fixe de vCPU, de mémoire et de GPU, semblable aux ressources que tu demandes à un ordonnanceur HPC. Lorsque tu téléverses un workflow, tu associes ses tailles, telles que `S` et `M`, à des profils, et chaque exécution choisit l'une de ces tailles. Le job s'exécute ensuite sur son propre nœud avec ce profil, et le conserve jusqu'à la fin du job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Profile | vCPUs | Memory (GB) | GPUs |\n"
"| - | - | - | - |\n"
"| `8x32` | 8 | 32 | None |\n"
"| `16x128` | 16 | 128 | None |\n"
"| `48x768` | 48 | 768 | None |\n"
"| `128x1500` | 128 | 1500 | None |\n"
"| `24x120x1l40s` | 24 | 120 | 1 L40S |\n"
"| `20x320x2a100` | 20 | 320 | 2 A100 |\n"
"| `80x1200x8a100` | 80 | 1200 | 8 A100 |\n"
"| `160x1792x8h100` | 160 | 1792 | 8 H100 |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Profil | vCPU | Mémoire (Go) | GPU |\n"
"| - | - | - | - |\n"
"| `8x32` | 8 | 32 | Aucun |\n"
"| `16x128` | 16 | 128 | Aucun |\n"
"| `48x768` | 48 | 768 | Aucun |\n"
"| `128x1500` | 128 | 1500 | Aucun |\n"
"| `24x120x1l40s` | 24 | 120 | 1 L40S |\n"
"| `20x320x2a100` | 20 | 320 | 2 A100 |\n"
"| `80x1200x8a100` | 80 | 1200 | 8 A100 |\n"
"| `160x1792x8h100` | 160 | 1792 | 8 H100 |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A profile ID has the form `{cpu}x{memory}`, with memory in GB, or `{cpu}x{memory}x{count}{gpu}` for a profile with GPUs. For example, `24x120x1l40s` has 24 vCPUs, 120 GB of memory, and one NVIDIA L40S GPU.\n"
msgstr "Un ID de profil a la forme `{cpu}x{memory}`, avec la mémoire en Go, ou `{cpu}x{memory}x{count}{gpu}` pour un profil avec GPU. Par exemple, `24x120x1l40s` a 24 vCPU, 120 Go de mémoire et un GPU NVIDIA L40S.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check available profiles {#check-available-profiles}"
msgstr "Vérifier les profils disponibles {#check-available-profiles}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see which profiles are available, call `compute_profiles()`:\n"
msgstr "Pour voir quels profils sont disponibles, appelle `compute_profiles()` :\n"

